lass=\"ico-16\">';\r\n      jQuery('.result_test_server_address_ng').html(`${icon} ${i18n.ConnectionTestFailed}`);\r\n    }\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction testInternalServerAddressNg() {\r\n  const baseUrl = window.location.origin;\r\n  const internalUrlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"internal_server_address_ng\"]')\r\n    .val();\r\n  const data = { url: internalUrlServerNg };\r\n\r\n  jQuery.ajax({\r\n    type: 'POST',\r\n    url: `${baseUrl}/centreon/api/latest/map/check-health`,\r\n    dataType: 'json',\r\n    contentType: 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\r\n    data: JSON.stringify(data),\r\n    success: () => {\r\n      const icon = '<img src=\"./img/icons/checked.png\" class=\"ico-16\">';\r\n      jQuery('.result_test_internal_server_address_ng')\r\n        .html(`${icon} ${i18n.ConnectionTestSuccessful}`);\r\n    },\r\n    error: () => {\r\n      const icon = '<img src=\"./img/icons/cross.png\" class=\"ico-16\">';\r\n      jQuery('.result_test_internal_server_address_ng')\r\n        .html(`${icon} ${i18n.ConnectionTestFailed}`);\r\n    }\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Management of inputs required or not for server addresses\r\n * via HTML 5 for the \"required\" before saving the form. \r\n * @param {boolean} isNgSelected \r\n */\r\nfunction enableInputRequired(isNgSelected) {\r\n  if (isNgSelected) {\r\n    jQuery('input[name=\"server_address_ng\"]').attr('required', true);\r\n    jQuery('input[name=\"server_address\"]').removeAttr('required');\r\n  } else {\r\n    jQuery('input[name=\"server_address_ng\"]').removeAttr('required');\r\n    jQuery('input[name=\"server_address\"]').attr('required', true);\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\n\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":869,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:03:12Z","content":"We have found the **exact source code** for that button in Centreon Web ([`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266-L281)).\n\nThis reveals why `tcpdump` captured 0 packets from the backend: **The backend never makes this call.**\n\n---\n\n### The Code Behind the Buttons\n\nIn [`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266-L295):\n\n```javascript\n// 1. \"MAP Engine server address\" button:\nfunction testServerAddressNg() {\n  const urlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"server_address_ng\"]').val();\n\n  jQuery.ajax({\n    type : 'GET',\n    url : `${urlServerNg}/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health`,\n    success: () => { /* Green Check */ }, \n    error: () => { /* Red X */ }\n  });\n}\n\n// 2. \"MAP server address as seen by Central\" button:\nfunction testInternalServerAddressNg() {\n  const baseUrl = window.location.origin;\n  const internalUrlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"internal_server_address_ng\"]').val();\n  const data = { url: internalUrlServerNg };\n\n  jQuery.ajax({\n    type: 'POST',\n    url: `${baseUrl}/centreon/api/latest/map/check-health`,  // <--- Sent to PHP backend!\n    ...\n```\n\n---\n\n### The Revelation\n\n1. **`MAP server address as seen by Central`** (Green check):\n   * Tested **server-side** by PHP on Central (`th2-centprop-be1`). It queries the internal network directly, which is why it succeeds.\n2. **`MAP Engine server address`** (Red X):\n   * Tested **client-side by your web browser** on your workstation via JavaScript AJAX!\n   * Your browser directly calls:\n     ```text\n     GET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### The 2 Exact Reasons Why Your Browser Fails\n\n#### 1. CORS Block (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)\n* Your browser is viewing the Centreon Web page on port **`443`** (`https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`).\n* The AJAX script calls port **`9443`** (`https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`).\n* Because the port is different (`443` vs `9443`), modern web browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge) treat this as a **Cross-Origin request**.\n* Browsers strictly **block** cross-origin AJAX calls unless Nginx returns CORS headers:\n  ```nginx\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS' always;\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'Authorization, Content-Type' always;\n  ```\n  Without these headers, your browser silently rejects the response and displays **Connection test failed**.\n\n#### 2. Workstation Hairpin NAT\n* Your browser resolves `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the public IP **`109.62.64.18`**.\n* If your PC is connected to the internal corporate LAN/VPN, traffic from your PC targeting the corporate public VIP `109.62.64.18:9443` is dropped by the corporate firewall (lack of NAT loopback / Hairpin NAT).\n\n---\n\n### How to Verify in 5 Seconds\n\n1. On the Centreon Web page, press **F12** in your browser to open **Developer Tools**.\n2. Go to the **Console** tab.\n3. Click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n4. You will see the exact red browser error, for example:\n   * `Access to XMLHttpRequest at 'https://map...:9443/.../health' from origin 'https://extranetclient...' has been blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.`\n   * Or: `net::ERR_CONNECTION_TIMED_OUT` (Firewall dropping packet from workstation to public IP).","thinking":"**Confirming Server Address Health**\n\nThe code snippet tests a server address by sending a GET request to a health endpoint. Success displays a confirmation message with a checkmark icon. This confirms the validity of the server address input field. The core logic now centers on verifying the URL's endpoint response.\n\n\n**Identifying CORS as the Cause**\n\nThe key difference lies in where the server address tests execute: one on the PHP backend, the other in the browser. The successful PHP-backend test suggests the problem lies with the browser's attempted access to an external server. Specifically, a cross-origin request (CORS) could be blocking the client-side test. This hypothesis is strong because the browser is attempting to access a different domain.\n\n\n**Analyzing CORS and Network Reachability**\n\nThe browser enforces CORS for AJAX calls to different domains or ports, explaining the observed behavior.  The server requires the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header for cross-origin requests.  If the server doesn't provide this header, the connection test fails immediately.\n\nNext, it is important to check the server address's IP, because the AJAX request to the server address is failing. Also, verifying if the target machine is reachable on the corporate network is an important step to take. Finally, we need to assess the target server endpoint by checking what `/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health` returns.\n\n\n"}
